## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests analyzed → 9 Critical findings, 2 Medium findings**

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (achieving high coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if every method is completely broken, as long as it doesn't throw.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — False Confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic — entire file)

All 10 tests methodically call every public method on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order. 5 out of 10 tests have **zero assertions**. The remaining 5 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`, which verifies almost nothing meaningful.

This is why bugs reach production despite 95% coverage — coverage only proves code was *executed*, not that it *works*.

#### 2. No Assertions (5 tests)

| Line | Method | What's untested |
|------|--------|-----------------|
| 17 | `AddProduct_Works` | Never verifies the product was actually stored |
| 33 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Never verifies the price actually changed |
| 39 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Never verifies the product was actually removed |
| 64 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Never verifies the count value |
| 69 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Never verifies prices were discounted |

**Fix for `AddProduct_Works` (line 17):**
```csharp
// BEFORE
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix for `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33):**
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix for `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39):**
```csharp
// AFTER
[TestMethod]
